{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Shaddai shall be</b> — it means shall be strong, like <b>the voice of Shaddai</b>." "<b>בצריך</b> — your silver." "<b>And silver of heights to you</b> — the matter is doubled according to convention, and <b>תועפות</b> means might and strength, like <b>the heights of mountains are His</b>; <b>like the heights of Re'em is His</b>." "Some say: <b>And Shaddai shall be בצריך</b> — according to its plain meaning, like <b>I am with him in distress</b>, and the first is more correct, to attach it to the end of the verse."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:26.591541556Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}